PostgreSQL via Docker Compose. Start it with `docker compose up -d`. The connection string is in `DATABASE_URL` (see `.env.example`).

The local `DATABASE_URL` ends with `?sslmode=disable` because the Docker database has no TLS. Keep `sslmode=disable` for local or other non-TLS databases only. Never copy the local `DATABASE_URL` to production.{{#if project.orm}}{{#unless (and (has "orm" "drizzle") (databaseBinding "hyperdrive") (has "deployment" "cloudflare"))}} The generated client connects with TLS and verifies the server certificate when `NODE_ENV=production`, unless `DATABASE_URL` sets `sslmode`, which always wins. A managed database (Neon, Supabase, RDS) keeps TLS with the connection string it provides.{{/unless}}{{/if}}
